ion of evidence-based medicine into NUTRICIÓN CLÍNICA emphasizes the importance of dietary interventions in the prevention and treatment of diseases, making it a cornerstone of modern healthcare practices. [Data: Entities (346); Relationships (719, 1521, 2530, 2511, 960, +more)]\n\n## The role of METABOLISMO in clinical nutrition\n\nMETABOLISMO encompasses all biochemical processes that occur within living organisms to maintain life, including digestion and nutrient absorption. It is closely related to nutrition and plays a crucial role in understanding the nutritional needs of individuals, particularly during specific conditions such as pregnancy and recovery from trauma. The relationship between NUTRICIÓN CLÍNICA and METABOLISMO highlights the necessity of understanding metabolic processes to optimize dietary interventions and improve patient outcomes. [Data: Entities (4835); Relationships (720, 14122, 14123, 10557, +more)]\n\n## Importance of specialized nutrition for burned and trauma patients\n\nNUTRICIÓN EN PACIENTES QUEMADOS Y TRAUMATOLÓGICOS focuses on the medical management and nutritional needs of patients who have suffered burns or severe trauma. This area of clinical nutrition is critical as these patients often have increased metabolic demands and require tailored nutritional support to aid in recovery. The involvement of specialized medical professionals in this field ensures that the unique dietary needs of these patients are met effectively. [Data: Entities (13178); Relationships (9515, 12116, 19386, 2502, +more)]\n\n## Cost-benefit analysis in clinical nutrition\n\nCOSTE-BENEFICIO refers to a method of analysis that evaluates the relationship between the costs associated with nutritional interventions and the benefits derived from them. This analysis is essential in clinical nutrition as it provides insights into the efficiency and effectiveness of various treatments, allowing healthcare providers to make informed decisions regarding resource allocation and patient care strategies. [Data: Entities (15950); Relationships (2548, 13174, 20389, 2546, +more)]\n\n## The role of medical professionals in clinical nutrition\n\nA network of medical professionals, including DRES. ALFONSO VIDAL CASARIEGO and DRA. MARÍA DOLORES BALLESTEROS POMAR, plays a vital role in the design and development of clinical nutrition products. Their expertise in clinical nutrition management and research contributes to advancements in dietary interventions and the overall improvement of patient care. The collaboration among these professionals enhances the quality and effectiveness of clinical nutrition practices. [Data: Entities (15790, 15794); Relationships (2537, 2540, 2541, 2542, +more)]\"\r\n\n\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n303,AGUA,\"AGUA refers to water, an essential fluid required for hydration and various bodily functions. It plays a critical role in cooking and baking, including the preparation of desserts. In healthcare settings, AGUA is vital for the hydration needs of hospitalized patients, with daily requirements typically ranging from 30 to 40 mL/kg. It is also used to dilute medications for proper delivery through enteral feeding tubes and is a key component in clinical nutrition products, affecting the hydration and stability of ingredients.\n\nThe recommended daily intake of AGUA varies based on body weight, age, and activity level, and it is crucial for maintaining hydration, especially during physical exercise, where it aids in cooling, nutrient delivery, and waste elimination. In patients undergoing hematopoietic transplants, monitoring the balance of AGUA is essential for their dietary needs. Additionally, AGUA is important for maintaining hydration and electrolyte balance in enteral nutrition.\n\nAGUA is a gluten-free beverage and is often assessed in nutritional evaluations for its critical role in overall health. It is also used for cleaning feeding tubes and ensuring patient oral hygiene. While AGUA can contain sodium, particularly in mineral waters, it is generally recommended that its consumption does not correlate with weight variations. Overall, AGUA is a vital nutrient necessary for life, contributing significantly to hydration and health, particularly in children.\",25\r\n13733,HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO 12 DE OCTUBRE,\"Hospital Universitario 12 de Octubre is a medical institution located in Madrid, Spain. It specializes in pediatrics, endocrinology, and clinical nutrition, providing a comprehensive range of healthcare services in these fields.\",14\r\n13055,SOCIEDAD ESPAÑOLA DE NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL,\"The Sociedad Española de Nutrición Parenteral y Enteral (SENPE) is an organization dedicated to establishing quality criteria for clinical nutrition. It plays a crucial role in providing recommendations for nutritional support specifically aimed at patients who require artificial nutrition. Through its efforts, SENPE aims to enhance the standards and practices related to parenteral and enteral nutrition in clinical settings.\",3\r\n5033,COSTE-EFECTIVIDAD,\"COSTE-EFECTIVIDAD refers to a comprehensive analysis used to evaluate the economic viability of various interventions aimed at achieving specific health outcomes. This analysis measures effectiveness in clinical terms, such as the cost per case of infections or the cost of life years gained. It plays a crucial role in the economic evaluation of enteral nutrition formulas, particularly highlighting their benefits for surgical patients. Additionally, coste-efectividad is essential for assessing the economic feasibility of home artificial nutrition within healthcare systems. It is also a significant factor when choosing between parenteral and enteral nutrition, as the costs associated with devices and care are generally higher for parenteral nutrition.\",3\r\n1692,KWASHIORKOR,\"Kwashiorkor is a severe form of malnutrition primarily resulting from a protein-deficient diet. It is often characterized by symptoms such as edema and growth failure, particularly in children. In addition to its primary association with protein deficiency, Kwashiorkor can also be linked to severe nutritional deficiencies, including low copper levels. Furthermore, this condition can impact lactase activity in infants and young children, potentially affecting their ability to digest lactose. Overall, Kwashiorkor represents a critical health issue related to inadequate protein intake and its associated complications.\",4\r\n16055,EVALUACIÓN DE OPORTUNIDADES,\"La evaluación de oportunidades implica valorar la viabilidad técnica, económica y comercial de los proyectos de innovación.\",3\r\n1691,MARASMO,\"Marasmo is a type of severe malnutrition characterized by insufficient caloric intake, which results in a specific clinical presentation. It is primarily caused by a deficiency of both calories and protein, leading to significant weight loss and muscle wasting. This condition reflects a critical state of undernutrition, where the body does not receive the necessary nutrients to maintain normal physiological functions.\",2\r\n16046,MILAGROS PÉREZ RODRÍGUEZ,\"Milagros Pérez Rodríguez is the Director of R&D and Quality at VEGENAT, S.A., overseeing the development of clinical nutrition products.\",2\r\n16047,ÁFRICA JIMÉNEZ JIMÉNEZ,\"África Jiménez Jiménez is the R&D Manager at VEGENAT, S.A., responsible for the research and development of nutrition products.\",2\r\n16019,SOCIEDAD ESPAÑOLA DE CALIDAD ASISTENCIAL,The Sociedad Española de Calidad Asistencial is an organization that collaborates in defining quality criteria for healthcare services.,2\r\n15787,JOSÉ ENRIQUE PALACIO ABIZANDA,Head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Universitario Ntra. Sra. de Candelaria in Tenerife.,2\r\n1787,PERFUSIONES ENDOVENOSAS,\"Intravenous infusions are administered to hospitalized patients for medication delivery, which also impacts their hydration and electrolyte balance.\